            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 36-year-old male, admitted on 08/07/2025 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever. Clinical examination revealed rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Laboratory workup confirmed leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient was promptly prepared for surgical intervention. A laparoscopic appendectomy was performed on 08/07/2025 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, the patient received intravenous fluids, analgesics, and prophylactic antibiotics. Wound healing was satisfactory, vital signs remained stable throughout, and bowel function resumed normally. The patient was mobilized early with physiotherapy support and discharged home on 10/07/2025 in good general condition. Please follow up in approximately one week. I remain available for any further questions.</div>"
            },
